Jihad Browser — webOS NPAPI plugin INPUT, the frozen plugin YAP commands, and the frame path
that makes ANIMATED plugin content run (addons R7).

Applies on top of 0005, 0008 and 0016-0023. Supersedes the earlier 0024, which carried only the
input half.

── INPUT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. npapi.h — NPEvent becomes Palm's real 48-byte event union on a headless XP_UNIX build
   instead of `typedef void*`. That typedef was not a harmless placeholder: NPRemoteEvent is a
   raw memcpy of sizeof(NPEvent), so the parent shipped four bytes of its own address space to
   the child. No event could ever have carried a payload. With a real POD the stock
   NPP_HandleEvent path carries a Palm event unmodified, with no paramtraits change.
2. nsPluginInstanceOwner.cpp — ProcessEvent gains the arm this toolkit never had. Its whole
   body was inside XP_MACOSX / XP_WIN / MOZ_X11, so on cairo-headless it reduced to
   `return eIgnore` and a windowless plugin got nothing for its entire lifetime. Mouse maps to
   npPalmPen{Down,Up,Move,Click,DoubleClick}, keys to npPalmKey{Down,Up,Press}, focus/blur to
   the npPalmSystemEvent pair, reusing the MOZ_X11 arm's plugin-local coordinate recipe and
   adding no zoom or scroll arithmetic of its own — which is what makes plugin input land where
   page content does.
3. PluginInstanceChild.{cpp,h} — drops the truncated private JihadNpPalm* mirrors for that
   NPEvent, asserts every offset against the libWebKitLuna address it was read from, and adds a
   capped input-delivery breadcrumb.
4. nsPluginHost.{cpp,h} — jihad_plugin_palm_spotlight, a MOZ_EXPORT'd C entry point (the
   jihad_offscreen_* precedent) so the daemon can deliver npPalmSpotlightStart/EndEvent for the
   frozen asyncCmdPluginSpotlight* commands. nsNPAPIPluginInstance::HandleEvent is neither
   exported nor virtual, so there is no other route.

── ANIMATION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5. nsPluginInstanceOwner.cpp — the windowless invalidate now names the PLUGIN's box instead of
   the whole widget. 0021 invalidated nearest->GetBounds() on the reasoning that the daemon
   repainted everything anyway; once the daemon learned to repaint only damaged rows, that
   reasoning inverted and a full-viewport damage box forced the expensive path on every frame.
6. PuppetWidget.{cpp,h} — accumulate the bounding box of everything invalidated since the last
   drain, exposed as jihad_offscreen_take_dirty_rect beside the existing flag, so the daemon can
   repaint 320x240 (~2 ms) instead of the whole viewport (~38 ms).
7. PluginInstanceChild.cpp — the Palm draw event always covers the WHOLE plugin surface. The
   PGContext is built for the full surface, so pairing it with a dstBuffer offset into the
   middle of that surface made the plugin's blit run off the end — SIGBUS in the plugin child
   the moment the host started sending partial invalidations. Palm's own host never sent a
   partial rect either.
8. PluginInstanceParent.cpp — a bounded RecvShow frame-rate line, so the rate frames actually
   cross the process boundary can be compared against the rate the plugin was asked to draw.

Device-measured with a purpose-built 30fps SWF (render/goanna/test/make-anim-swf.py): the
plugin draws at 27-31 fps, every frame crosses IPC, and the card composites at 28.3 fps with an
average frame gap of 31-35 ms. Before this work the same content drew at 30 fps inside the
plugin and reached the screen 5 times in 25 seconds.

